==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qual|UK}} {{l|en|metabolise}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|μετᾰβολή||change, mutation}} + {{m|en|-ize}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɪˈtæbəˌlaɪz/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|me|tab|o|lize}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|biology|intransitive}} To [[undergo]] [[metabolism]].
# {{lb|en|biology|transitive}} To [[cause]] a [[substance]] to undergo metabolism.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2004|author=Walter C. Willett|title=News About What You Drink|journal=Mother Earth News|passage=Among the many types of juice, grapefruit stands out from the pack because it changes the way some people absorb and '''metabolize''' different drugs.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2004–05|author=Dustin Stephens|author2=Robert Dudley|title=The Drunken Monkey Hypothesis|journal={{w|Journal of Natural History}}|page=43|passage=The genes in question encode two enzymes that '''metabolize''' alcohol and its breakdown products; the two enzymes are known as alcohol dehydrogenase and aldehyde dehydrogenase.}}
# {{lb|en|biology|transitive}} To [[produce]] a substance using metabolism.
# {{lb|en|by extension|transitive}} To [[absorb]] and [[process]] as if by metabolism.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1887-03-18|author=L. H.|title=Zoölogy in the college course|journal=[[w:Science (journal)|Science]]|volume=IX|number=215|page=264|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=IdxRAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA264|passage=We believe this to be the true way to teach zoölogy, for we doubt the value to a man of a mass of indefinite ill-digested text-book information. Occasionally an omnivore can take in every thin, and digest and so '''metabolize''' it as to organize it into healthy mental tissue. They are, however, the few.}}

